rt raters call the race Solid or Safe Democratic", "Prediction markets price Shapiro's win probability at 96 to 98 percent", "Shapiro vastly outraises and outspends Garrity, who trails in name recognition"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Shapiro ahead by 17 to 20 points, expert raters unanimously rate the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and markets price a Shapiro win at 96 to 98 percent. Combined with his incumbency and fundraising edge, the evidence points to a comfortable double-digit victory.", "watch": "A late polling shift or major campaign surprise could narrow the margin, though nothing in the current evidence suggests the outcome itself is in doubt.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Josh Shapiro seeks a second term against State Senator Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Pennsylvania is roughly even in partisan lean, but Shapiro enters with strong incumbency advantages, a large fundraising edge, and consistently high approval in polling.\n\nEvery independent poll since June has shown Shapiro leading by at least 17 points, including September surveys of likely voters at 17 and 20 points. All seven major race raters classify the contest as Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Shapiro's win probability at 96 to 98 percent. Garrity has struggled with fundraising and name recognition, and recent coverage emphasizes the lopsided nature of the race rather than genuine competition.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 20.0}, {"da